@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamAudreyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Audrey Sierends";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Audrey Sierends</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    An F&amp;B entrepreneur whose work is guided by empathy, impact,
                    and the belief that business can create meaningful opportunities for others.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>F&amp;B Entrepreneur</span>
                    <span>Impact</span>
                    <span>Empathy</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/audrey.jpg" alt="Audrey Sierends">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">Her Background</p>
                <h3>Growing Up Around Food, Business, and People</h3>

                <p>
                    Hi everyone, my name is Audrey Sierends. I am an F&amp;B entrepreneur
                    based in Shanghai and Malang.
                </p>

                <p>
                    I grew up in a family involved in the food and beverage industry, so from
                    a young age, I was surrounded by how businesses operate and how people
                    connect through food.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Over time, I began to see that business is not just about selling a product,
                    but about creating experiences and relationships.
                </p>

                <p>
                    To learn more about my journey, please visit
                    <a href="https://audreysierends.squarespace.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                        audreysierends.squarespace.com
                    </a>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>Her Focus</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Food and beverage entrepreneurship</li>
                    <li>Community impact</li>
                    <li>Opportunity creation</li>
                    <li>Empathy-driven business</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Responsibility</p>
                <h3>Seeing Privilege as Something to Share</h3>

                <p>
                    As Audrey grew older, she became more aware of the privilege she had,
                    whether through the opportunities she was given or the environment she
                    was raised in.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Instead of seeing privilege as something to keep, she began to see it as
                    a responsibility to share. That belief continues to shape the way she
                    approaches everything she builds.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Impact</p>
                <h3>Business as a Platform for Change</h3>

                <p>
                    Today, Audrey sees business as a platform for impact. Through Kopi Cinta
                    and other initiatives, she focuses on creating something that goes beyond
                    transactions.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Her goal is to bring people together, create opportunities for those who
                    are often overlooked, and build a sense of connection and belonging.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>Her Reflection</h3>

            <p>
                For Audrey, what matters is not only growth in numbers, but the depth of
                impact—how much we can truly make a difference in someone’s life, no matter
                how small it may seem.
            </p>

            <p>
                She is still learning every day, but one thing she holds onto is this:
                whatever we build should come from a place of empathy, and should always
                give back more than it takes.
            </p>
        </div>

        <br />

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>